Weather Rescue Brazil — licensing
=================================

Three different things live in this repository, and they are licensed
differently on purpose.

1. THE OBSERVATIONS ARE NOT OURS TO LICENCE.

   The measurements themselves come from nineteenth-century Brazilian
   government publications and are in the public domain (Lei 9.610; the corpus
   is 1883-1890). Anyone may use the numbers themselves for any purpose. No
   licence here restricts that, and no licence could.

2. THE TRANSCRIPTIONS, VERDICTS AND ANNOTATIONS — CC BY-NC 4.0

   What this project added: reading the printed tables into machine-readable
   values, the per-row quality verdicts, the corrections, and the provenance.
   Those are licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0
   International.

   You may share and adapt them for any NON-COMMERCIAL purpose, provided you
   attribute the project and this licence. Commercial use requires permission.

   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/legalcode

3. THE CODE — PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0

   Everything in `src/`, `scripts/`, `tests/` and `profiles/`.

   You may use it for any noncommercial purpose, including research, teaching
   and personal projects. You may not use it commercially.

   https://polyformproject.org/licenses/noncommercial/1.0.0/

   (The usual software licences — MIT, Apache — permit commercial use, so they
   are not what is written here. PolyForm Noncommercial is a software licence
   that says what you asked for, in a form lawyers and tooling both recognise.)

4. THE MODEL WEIGHTS — CC BY-NC 4.0

   The LoRA adapters and the packaged quantised model. Same terms as the
   transcriptions: non-commercial, with attribution.

   Note the base model is Qwen3.5-2B under its own licence (Apache-2.0 at the
   time of writing); this licence covers the adapter, not the base.

ATTRIBUTION
-----------

   Acervo: Biblioteca Digital de Obras Raras do Observatório Nacional, via
   DocVirt. Digitalizado e transcrito pelo projeto Weather Rescue Brazil.

The collection asks for this string and it travels with every downloaded page
in `data/raw/docvirt/*/*.json`. Please carry it.

A NOTE ON WHY NON-COMMERCIAL
----------------------------

This was a deliberate choice by the project owner, not an oversight, and it is
worth stating plainly what it costs: non-commercial terms make the dataset
ineligible for some open-data services and for C3S ingestion in some channels.
If that trade-off turns out to be the wrong one, changing it later is a licence
change and nothing else — the data does not have to be re-derived.
